From 9072030d105393aacc48f331779b5da4e4fc644b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Williams <patrick@stwcx.xyz>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:46:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/33] log-create: add --extend to attach extension data to
 events

Add an option to `log-create` as `--extend` which act as the equivalent
of `event.extend(...)`.  This allows users to mock extension data, or
for scripts to induce it.

Currently `Extension.CPER.{Processed,Raw}` are supported but additional
extensions can be added in a simple manner.

Tested:
Used two `--extend` flags to create an event and verified the
extensions landed in the resulting entry:

```
log-create \
  -j '{"NUMBER_OF_LOGS":5}' \
  --extend xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed \
          '{"DiagnosticDataType":"xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER","Oem":{"Vendor":"{\"key\":\"value\"}"}}' \
  --extend xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Raw \
          '{"Data":[1,2,3]}' \
  xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Cleared
/xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/4279542443
```

The entry persisted the payloads in additionalData._EXTENSIONS:

```
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed =>
  {"DiagnosticDataType": "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER",
   "NotificationType": "", "Oem": {"Vendor": "{\"key\":\"value\"}"},
   "SectionType": ""}
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Raw =>
  {"Data": [1, 2, 3]}
```

